  "body": "> An object image is not origin-clean if, switching on image's type:\r\n>\r\n> HTMLOrSVGImageElement\r\n> image's current request's image data is CORS-cross-origin.\r\n>\r\n> HTMLVideoElement\r\n> image's media data is CORS-cross-origin.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#the-image-argument-is-not-origin-clean\r\n\r\n[CORS-cross-origin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-cross-origin) is defined for a [response](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response). But [image data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#images-processing-model:img-req-data) and [media data](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#media-data) are not defined to be responses. Therefore, CORS-cross-origin is undefined for these.\r\n\r\nMedia data can come from a [media provider object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#media-provider-object), where there is no fetch.\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#loading-the-media-resource:media-data-5",
